Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:28:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Ship built-in apps with MOSdesk and add per-user folders

Built-in apps: every mosdesk/apps/<name>.c (or <name>/ with a main.c) is
built as mos_<name>.run and installed to 0:/programs. The first one is
MOS Edit (apps/edit.c), an easyui text editor. The mosdesk package now
installs at 0:/ (MOSdesk itself under programs/mosdesk) so apps can land
in 0:/programs. The desktop shows mos_edit.run as "Edit", and text files
opened from the desktop or Files open in it.

Users: first-run setup asks for a username and creates
0:/users/<username>/{Documents,Pictures,Desktop}. Home opens that folder,
everything in Desktop appears as desktop icons (re-read twice a second),
and the home and its folders are protected from rename/delete. Existing
installs are asked for a username once, after sign-in. Settings files
from before this change are migrated (icon slots grow from 34 to 66).

Also bumps the Minimal-OS-SDK submodule to the commit with easyui, which
the editor needs, and rebuilds the committed mosWM outputs.

